reply.body:
Specifically, I think `Executor` should be a non-static inner class of `MetadataIndexAliasesService` so that there's no need to explicitly pass around any references to the `MetadataIndexAliasesService`. Something like this perhaps?

```
    class Executor extends SimpleBatchedAckListenerTaskExecutor<ApplyAliasActions> {
        @Override
        public Tuple<ClusterState, ClusterStateAckListener> executeTask(ApplyAliasActions applyAliasActions, ClusterState clusterState) throws Exception {
            return Tuple.tuple(applyAliasActions(clusterState, applyAliasActions.request().actions()), applyAliasActions.getAckListener());
        }
    }
```

